/target
*.log
# Compiled MQL5 binaries (build artifacts of bridge/mt5/*.mq5)
*.ex5
# Local feed/asset override (see README: ./quantick.toml or QUANTICK_CONFIG)
/quantick.toml
# User indicator scripts, created beside the app on first run
/indicators
# The indicator set the app remembers between runs
/indicators-state.toml
# Python bytecode from the design lab
__pycache__/

# Server-time offset the MT5 bridge measures and remembers (per machine).
.quantick_bridge_cache.json
# Simulated paper-trading history, written by the app at runtime
/paper-trades
# The drawing presets the app remembers between runs (PR #94 follow-up)
/quantick-drawing-presets.toml
# Which chart layers the app was last showing (the right-click layer menu)
/chart-layers.toml
# The saved chart layouts the app remembers between runs
/layouts.toml
# The paper sidecar: journal folder pick and cmd-trading settings, per machine
/paper-state.toml
# Instruments added from the app's source picker (its own header says so)
/quantick-symbols.toml
crates/app/indicators-state.toml

# Footprint settings the app writes at runtime (like chart-layers.toml).
footprint-settings.toml
footprint-presets.toml
indicator-presets.toml

# The *live* goal file `mission` writes. It describes the session in progress
# and cites line numbers that same session is changing, so it is stale before
# it is read. The `GOAL-archive-<slug>.md` it becomes at the end is tracked
# (21 of them are) — that one is a record of a shipped change, this one is
# scratch.
.claude/GOAL.md

# Session scratch: the investigation record before it becomes an archive.
.claude/laudo-scratch.md

# Evidence logs are the point of the evidence folder: a measurement whose log
# is ignored is a claim with a dead link under it.
!.claude/evidence/**/*.log

# Screenshots under the evidence folder: the capture's hash written into the
# text file beside it is the evidence a reader can check; the pixels are the
# trader's local proof and cost 10 MB to carry for everyone else.
.claude/evidence/**/*.png
